      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "DOOR BUSTER (3) is the one to beat after winning first-up in BM58+ company at this track, overcoming a slow beginning and some difficulty getting clear before charging home to beat CHIPILLY. Her record at this venue is strong, and four wins from seven starts around 1200m gives the profile real substance. CHIPILLY (8) was only beaten a head in that same race and is the clear danger, especially with recent form that has her rated among the sharper hopes. MORF (2) brings winning momentum after successive victories at this track, the latest by two lengths in BM58+ grade, and the returning winning rider is a positive. JUST FAMOUS (1) resumed with a sound third in BM66+ company, has a reliable track-and-distance record, and the apprentice claim helps him stay in the minor-winning mix. SPANGLEDSTAR (5) is better than she showed last start and can bounce back to form.",
